<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" id="m49301-menu-excerpt"><example id="Example_01_01_01"><exercise id="fs-id1165137414052"><problem id="fs-id1165137559269">
<title>Determining If Menu Price Lists Are Functions</title>
 <para id="fs-id1165137436464">The coffee shop menu, shown in <link target-id="Figure_01_01_004" /> consists of items and their prices.</para><list id="fs-id1165137646341" list-type="enumerated" number-style="lower-alpha"><item><span class="token">ⓐ</span> Is price a function of the item?</item>
<item><span class="token">ⓑ</span> Is the item a function of the price?</item>
</list>

<figure id="Figure_01_01_004" class="small">
 <media id="fs-id1165137705861" alt="A menu of donut prices from a coffee shop where a plain donut is $1.49 and a jelly donut and chocolate donut are $1.99.">
<image mime-type="image/jpg" src="../../media/CNX_Precalc_Figure_01_01_004.jpg" />
</media>
</figure>

</problem>
<solution id="fs-id1165135419802">

<list id="fs-id1165137643241" list-type="enumerated" number-style="arabic" class="circled"><item><span class="token">ⓐ</span> Let’s begin by considering the input as the items on the menu. The output values are then the prices. See <link target-id="Figure_01_01_027" />.

<figure id="Figure_01_01_027" class="medium">
 <media id="fs-id1165135253831" alt="A menu of donut prices from a coffee shop where a plain donut is $1.49 and a jelly donut and chocolate donut are $1.99.">
<image mime-type="image/jpg" src="../../media/CNX_Precalc_Figure_01_01_027.jpg" />
</media>
</figure>

<para id="fs-id1165135532324">Each item on the menu has only one price, so the price is a function of the item.</para>
 </item>
 <item><span class="token">ⓑ</span> Two items on the menu have the same price. If we consider the prices to be the input values and the items to be the output, then the same input value could have more than one output associated with it. See <link target-id="Figure_01_01_028" />.

<figure id="Figure_01_01_028" class="medium">
 <media id="fs-id1165135187276" alt="Association of the prices to the donuts.">
<image mime-type="image/jpg" src="../../media/CNX_Precalc_Figure_01_01_028.jpg" />
</media>
</figure>
 <para id="fs-id1165137754835">Therefore, the item is a not a function of price.</para>
</item>
</list></solution>
</exercise></example></document>